<title>POLAND: Agros prices issue at PLN 70 per share.</title>
<headline>Agros prices issue at PLN 70 per share.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food trader and producer Agros Holding SA has set the book-building price of its 2.425-million-share issue at 70 zlotys each, the company said in a statement on Monday.  </p>
<p> Issuer:				   Agros Holding SA</p>
<p> Type of issue:			  shares</p>
<p> Priced at (PLN):			70</p>
<p> (Previous) Pricing Range:	   65-80</p>
<p> No of Shares Offered:		 2.425 miliion</p>
<p> No of Shares Outstanding:	   8,575,000</p>
<p> Lead Manager:			   Creditanstalt Securities SA</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:		     n/a</p>
<p> Use Of Proceeds:			boost productivity and buy</p>
<p>					     new firms</p>
<p> Tranches:			    No of Shares  Subscription</p>
<p>					  Offered	 Period</p>
<p>selected institutional</p>
<p>		  investors:	1.24 million	   March 20-21</p>
<p> open				 300,000	    March 20-26</p>
<p> rights			     890,000	    March 20-26</p>
<p> Earnings Data		1997 forecast	  1996</p>
<p>(in million of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:			na		    32.0</p>
<p> Pre-tax			    na		    46.3</p>
<p> Sales:			     na		    94.8</p>
<p> Group net profit:	   81.3		     49.0</p>
<p> Group pre-tax		    na		    84.6</p>
<p> Group sales:		   1.55 bln		 1.24 bln</p>
<p>Main Shareholder:</p>
<p>Investment corporation  Towarzystwo Inwestycyjne Grupy Agros SA with 47.5 percent of shares and 81.3 percent of shareholder votes as of November 22, 1996. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
